
Artificial Neural Networks (ANN) – Regression & Classification

This repository contains implementations of Artificial Neural Networks (ANN) for both Regression and Classification problems using Python.

It demonstrates how neural networks can be applied to solve different types of machine learning tasks with practical examples.

 Project Structure
├── ANN_Regression.ipynb       # ANN model for regression problem
├── ANN_classification.ipynb   # ANN model for classification problem
└── README.md                  # Project documentation

Features
Implementation of ANN from scratch using libraries
Covers both:
🔹 Regression tasks (predict continuous values)
🔹 Classification tasks (predict categories)
Data preprocessing and normalization
Model training and evaluation
Visualization of results

 Technologies Used
Python 
NumPy
Pandas
Matplotlib / Seaborn
TensorFlow / Keras (or specify what you used)
 ANN for Regression
Description:

This notebook demonstrates how ANN can be used to predict continuous numerical values.

Steps Covered:
Data preprocessing
Feature scaling
Model building using ANN
Training the model
Evaluation using metrics like:
Mean Squared Error (MSE)
Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE)
 ANN for Classification
Description:

This notebook demonstrates classification using ANN.

Steps Covered:
Data preprocessing
Encoding categorical variables
Model building
Training and validation
Evaluation using:
Accuracy
Confusion Matrix
